Masuda-san.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.240
For a moment, I thought you 
were some kind of creeper.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:33.700
A creeper?! I'm just an upstanding citizen 
who happens to be a little playful!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.230
You came from my school. Were you working?

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:44.230
Yup. Just finished having a meeting 
about shooting the graduation ceremony.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.230
I'm gonna be helping out again.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.960
Say, Ichika-chan, are you hungry?

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:52.450
A little bit...

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.740
Then let's go get tea for real.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.600
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:01.470
Man, I'm starving! Down the hatch!

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:05.370
Masuda-san, this isn't really 
tea. It's pretty much food.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.360
Hey, don't worry about the minor details.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:15.880
Here you go.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:20.750
Thanks...

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:23.500
Hey, don't tell Ryo about today!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:29.040
If he finds out I had lunch with 
you alone, he'll wring my neck!

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.760
Wring...

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:33.510
You've
got
guts...

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:33.510
Oh? You had lunch
with Ichika-san?

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.460
I wouldn't put it past him.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.240
<i>Lunch with Ichika-san... 
Lunch with Ichika-san...</i>

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:33.510
True...

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.830
Well? Like it?

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:40.020
Yes, it's great.

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.270
Whew, good. Your forehead 
wrinkles finally disappeared.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:47.770
D-Did I look that intense?

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.230
You looked really deep in thought.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:54.470
<i>I guess he was worried about me. 
Masuda-san is pretty mature after all.</i>

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.240
Maybe I'll get some yakisoba, too.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.080
A limited-edition Valentine's Day dessert?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:05.750
Could it be you were deep in thought 
about Valentine's Day, Ichika-chan?

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.430
Whoa! Are you okay?

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:09.560
Here's some water.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.630
<i>How can everyone tell?</i>

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.960
<i>Is it just showing on my face?</i>

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.100
Yes...

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.200
I see. Valentine's, huh?

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.260
Oh, how sweet. Bittersweet like chocolate.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:26.680
Like chocolate?

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.350
So...

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.780
are you getting Ryo something?!

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:32.290
I-I plan to... Even though I don't want to.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:34.880
Yeah, that's definitely 
what I expected to hear.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.130
But I don't know exactly what to get him.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:40.260
Ah, so that's it.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.080
Yes.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.330
I see.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:47.580
Well, for Ryo, you might want to get 
something that's not chocolate.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.080
Huh?

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:53.170
He's super popular, so he got endless 
amounts of chocolate when he was in school.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.500
I figured.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.890
And when were in our second year of 
middle school, on Valentine's Day,

00:17:57.890 --> 00:18:00.950
I'm not sure if someone had a grudge or what,

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:06.300
but one of the chocolates he 
got had a clump of hair in it.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:07.090
What?!

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:14.110
I happened to be there when it happened, 
and it seemed to cause him some trauma.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:18.920
Ever since then, he hasn't accepted 
Valentine's chocolates from anyone.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:22.920
If they were from someone anonymous, 
he just threw them away.

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.870
Does Rio know about that?

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:30.880
He asked me not to tell anyone, so he 
probably hasn't told Rio-chan, either.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:34.540
Wait! Don't tell Ryo or 
Rio-chan that I told you this!

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.550
Please!

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.880
Everything about
today is a secret!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:36.880
You got it.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:42.240
And it's been ten years since then, 
so I'm not sure how he is now.

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:47.280
Um... So what was Ryo-san 
like as a teenager?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.270
Curious?

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:51.370
Oh, no! I didn't mean for it 
to sound deep or anything.

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:55.090
Well, let's see... In high school,

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:59.330
Ryo didn't try to fit in or hang 
out with the class or anything.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:03.120
I figured he was a good guy, 
so I hung out with him.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:09.360
But there were other guys who complained, 
saying he wasn't much of a team player.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.260
And he stood out even more in a bad way 
because he was super popular with the girls.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:20.570
But we had a reunion recently,

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:24.240
and our classmates we hadn't seen 
in forever saw Ryo and said,

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:27.550
"Wow, he's changed! He's way more friendly!"

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:31.680
And I'm sure one thing that made him 
that way was meeting you, Ichika-chan.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.290
Huh?!

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:37.890
Man, the power of love is 
just amazing sometimes!

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:41.120
In a good way and in a bad 
way, man, I'm really sorry...

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:42.070
It's okay.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.600
I know I said a lot, but to be honest,

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:48.590
I'm sure Ryo would be happy to get 
anything from you, even chocolate.

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:51.080
Rio told me the same thing.

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:54.670
Did I end up confusing you even more? Sorry.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:57.040
Oh, no. I'm glad I got your opinion.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:02.430
I could tell that you wanted Ryo-san 
to have a nice Valentine's Day.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:09.010
When you say it like that, 
it's super embarrassing! Please stop!

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.680
<i>He's actually embarrassed.</i>

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:18.210
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:14.340
By the way, I absolutely love chocolate, 
so wink, wink, nudge, nudge.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.100
Wait, did you just laugh it off?

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.610
<i>Something that's not chocolate...</i>

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:24.700
<b>Chocolate</b>

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:29.430
<i>If he has memories like that, it's probably 
better that I don't get him food.</i>

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.650
<i>A plushie?</i>

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.040
<i>He wouldn't want that...</i>

00:20:34.390 --> 00:20:35.980
<b>Forward World X</b>

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.360
<i>A book?</i>

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:38.440
<i>But it'd be so hard to pick the right one...</i>

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:42.220
<i>A tie clip? I just got him one.</i>

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:48.160
<i>I wonder if I'd know what would make 
Ryo-san happy if I were more mature...</i>

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:51.220
<i>Maybe it shouldn't be a thing, but...</i>

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.640
An action...

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:00.700
<i>Hang on a second! What the 
heck was I just thinking?!</i>

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.860
<i>Nope, nope, nope! 
Not happening, no way! What?!</i>

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.930
<i>Am I really thinking that'd 
make Ryo-san happy?!</i>

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:08.470
<i>I'm getting way too full of myself! 
What's wrong with me?</i>

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:11.580
<i>I've been so weird ever since I met Ryo-san!</i>

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.440
<i>Ugh...</i>

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:22.840
Just five more days...

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:25.430
Ryo-san

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.440
His timing is too on point.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:32.770
Besides, this Valentine's Day 
is between you and my brother.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:35.850
Well, for Ryo, you might want to get 
something that's not chocolate.

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:42.300
Hello?

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:44.810
<i>Ichika-san, good evening! It is I, Ryo!</i>

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:46.220
Yes, I'm aware of that.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.450
<i>Well, I'm honored.</i>

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.830
Only five more days until Valentine's—

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:51.700
Ryo-san.

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:55.790
I'm going to head over there 
the morning of the 14th,

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.960
so could you make some time for 
me before you head to work?

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.470
<b>Valentine's Day</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
"The Person I Love Is..."

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.410
Next time, "The Person I Love Is..."
